WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:02.752
You're going spying?

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:06.464
I’m going to see some history that is happening today.

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:08.049
Well Hello, I’m Jane Lynch.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:09.342
Hi! I’m Lacey Chabert.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.803
Hey There! It’s Beanie Feldstein and I play Harriet M. Welsch

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:14.597
in the new&nbsp;Series Harriet the Spy. The character you may

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:16.516
already know and love&nbsp;but you’ve never seen our

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.684
fearless heroine quite like this.

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:23.940
I play Ole Golly, Harriet’s nanny and mentor.

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:27.736
Remember: life is a struggle and a good spy never quits.

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:31.031
I play Marion Hawthorne, Harriet’s classmate, and well, whatever

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.240
you’ve heard about Marion,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.908
I promise you don’t know the whole story.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.369
She’s a mean, rotten person who Janie and I

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.954
will someday get revenge on.

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:40.832
Here’s things you didn’t know about Harriet the Spy.

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:44.919
Harriet’s absolute&nbsp;favorite food is tomato sandwiches,

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:46.713
just white bread, tomato and mayonnaise.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.882
Her favorite color is red, because

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.592
it’s the color of her signature hoodie.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:53.762
Her worst enemy is Marion Hawthorne.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.556
I finished early so if anyone is still struggling,

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.725
I can, of course, help&nbsp;them out.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.435
Ugh buzz off Marion!

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:01.978
Marion wins at everything.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:04.439
I won with the word onomatopoeia.&nbsp;

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.066
Marion has excellent taste in fashion.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:07.108
Tres chic, no?

00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:09.944
But you better not wear the same thing that she’s wearing.

00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:12.489
She does&nbsp;not consider imitation the highest form of flattery.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.742
Please tell me that coat isn’t made by Smithers of London.

00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:18.161
Marion and Harriet were friends when they were younger.&nbsp;

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:19.829
Time to grow up, Harriet!

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:21.372
They couldn’t be more different.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:25.460
When Harriet has questions, Ole Golly always has the answers.

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:29.255
And&nbsp;there’s a lot you might not know about Ole Golly.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.342
She always knows the right thing to say.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:36.054
To be a writer, you need to see and know everything.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.723
She’s book-smart and street-smart.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.683
Hey, watch where you’re going!

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:43.186
Her middle name is Willa.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.106
Willa? What kind of a name is that anyway?

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.441
Well, it’s better than being a Myrtle!

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.276
She has some things to learn, too.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:55.657
Ole Golly, I don’t just want to be a writer – I want to be a great writer.

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:58.159
Well that means you’ve got to know everything.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:00.870
You might think you know Harriet, but like every good spy,

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.205
she’s got&nbsp;more up her sleeve.

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:07.794
I’m Harriet M. Welsch, and I will witness history in the making!

